# Vue Router runs in history mode, so every path has to be served index.html
# and routed client-side. Without this, any URL entered directly is a 404 -
# including /callback, which Auth0 redirects to after login, so the sign-in
# flow cannot complete.
#
# Both Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file from the published
# directory, which is why the rule lives here rather than in netlify.toml: one
# source of truth that survives the move between hosts.
#
# Files that exist are served in preference to this rule on both hosts, so it
# does not shadow /config.json or the hashed bundles.
/*    /index.html   200
